    <div id="search_lite_green_background" name="gene_model_downloads">
      <h2>Gene Model Downloads</h2>
      <p>
        The current gene model set for the representative maize genome, 
        m-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0 (B73 v5\) is Zm00001eb.1.
      </p>
<!--
      <p><span class="error"></p>
-->
      <p>
        <br>
        <img src="/images/mgdb_logo_sm.png" height=40>
        <br>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0_Zm00001eb.1.gff3.gz">Zm00001eb.1 gene model GFF</a><br>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0_Zm00001eb.1.cdna.fa.gz">Zm00001eb.1 gene model cDNA fasta</a><br>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0_Zm00001eb.1.cds.fa.gz">Zm00001eb.1 gene model CDS fasta</a><br>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0_Zm00001eb.1.gene.fa.gz">Zm00001eb.1 gene model genomic fasta</a><br>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0_Zm00001eb.1.protein.fa.gz">Zm00001eb.1 gene model protein fasta</a><br>
      </p>
      <br><br>
        
  <!-- CROSS-REFERENCES -->
        <a name="xref"></a>
        <div>
          <span style="font-family: Verdana, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 120%; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px;">
            Gene model cross-references and pan-genes
          </span>
<!--
          <p><span class="error"></span></p>
-->
          <p>
            Please note that there is not a 1-to-1 correspondence between all  
            gene models in all annotations. Some gene models are unique to
            specific genome assemblies, some have been split or merged
            between annotation or assembly versions, some direct associations may be 
            difficult to calculate, so multiple gene models that are similar in 
            sequence and position may be listed. And some gene models may be similar in
            sequence but do not appear in the same syntenic locations. 
            <br>
            <b id="gm_assoc_expand">+</b> 
            <a href="#xref" onclick="javascript:simple_toggle('gm_assoc_expand', 'gm_assoc_div'\);">Click to learn more.</a>
          </p>
          <div id="gm_assoc_div" style="margin-left:20px;display:none">
            The rules for associating gene models across assemblies require not 
            only close sequence similarity, but also that they both appear in 
            syntenic positions. Because of this, there are gene models that are 
            not associated with all gene models in the current representative 
            assembly annotation in spite of exact or near exact sequence 
            similarity. This is often due to unplaced scaffolds that contain 
            gene models.
            <br><br>
            There are multiple ways to define and generate a pan-genome. Here we use 
            "pan-gene" to mean to an analysis of multiple genome annotations to group 
            gene models by sequence similarity and syntenic position, to identify core 
            gene models (present in all annotations\) and to identify orphan gene models 
            (present in only one\). 
          </div>
          <br>
          <img src="/images/mgdb_logo_sm.png" height=40>
          <br>
          <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/B73_gene_xref/">Gene
          model associations across all B73 assemblies</a>.
          <br>
<!--
          <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/MaizeGDB_maize_pangene_2020_08.tsv.gz">Complete 
          list of pan-genes across genomes hosted by MaizeGDB</a>.
-->
          <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/Pan-Zea">Current pan-gene data</a><br>
<!--
          <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/archive">Older pan-gene versions</a>
-->
          <br>
        </div>
        <br>
        
  <!-- OLDER GENE MODEL DOWNLOADS -->
